WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.807 --> 00:00:13.793
Hi, I’m Evan Carmichael and welcome to another edition of Modeling the Masters.

00:00:14.123 --> 00:00:16.619
I believe that the fastest and most effective way

00:00:16.815 --> 00:00:17.846
to grow your business

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.797
is to model the strategies of people who’ve already done what you’re trying to do.

00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:23.791
So today we're going to look at how a young man

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:25.520
who couldn't hold down a steady job

00:00:25.762 --> 00:00:27.261
and couldn't get his mind off

00:00:27.521 --> 00:00:29.117
of thinking about hunting and fishing

00:00:29.164 --> 00:00:32.612
turned his passion into a business and would go on to be named

00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:37.564
one of the Top Ten Entrepreneurs of the 20th Century by the Wall Street Journal.

00:00:37.793 --> 00:00:39.683
This is the story of L.L. Bean

00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:42.640
and the top 3 lessons that you can learn from his success.

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:47.334
Leon Leonwood Bean was an inventor

00:00:47.461 --> 00:00:50.701
author, outdoor enthusiast, and founder of the company

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:51.271
L.L. Bean

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:52.883
As a young man

00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:55.586
Bean couldn't hold a steady job and drifted from place to place.

00:00:55.935 --> 00:00:58.131
He would much rather be out hunting and fishing

00:00:58.325 --> 00:00:59.618
than working for someone else.

00:00:59.889 --> 00:01:01.540
After a series of outdoor expeditions,

00:01:01.715 --> 00:01:04.327
Bean returned home with his feet soaking wet

00:01:04.475 --> 00:01:06.897
because there wasn't a good shoe that could keep them dry.

00:01:07.105 --> 00:01:10.283
He set out to solve the problem by visiting a local cobbler

00:01:10.514 --> 00:01:12.515
and creating a new shoe for outdoorsmen.

00:01:12.837 --> 00:01:14.740
He called it the Maine Hunting Shoe.

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:17.698
Bean got a list of hunting license holders,

00:01:17.842 --> 00:01:19.537
set up shop in his brother's basement

00:01:19.728 --> 00:01:22.393
and drafted a letter to be sent by mail to his list.

00:01:23.266 --> 00:01:25.052
Bean wrote, "Outside of your gun,

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:28.076
nothing is so important to your outfit as your foot-wear."

00:01:28.935 --> 00:01:30.954
You cannot expect success hunting deer or moose

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:33.066
if your feet are not properly dressed."

00:01:33.296 --> 00:01:34.898
The letter was a success

00:01:35.278 --> 00:01:36.876
and he sold 100 pairs

00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:40.103
only to have 90 of them returned because they broke apart.

00:01:40.603 --> 00:01:42.722
Bean refunded his customers the money

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:46.298
took out a loan to modify the design and began selling again.

00:01:47.516 --> 00:01:49.535
By the time Bean died in 1967

00:01:49.996 --> 00:01:52.597
company sales had passed $4 million per year

00:01:52.886 --> 00:01:54.483
and the Wall Street Journal named him

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.378
one of the Top Ten Entrepreneurs of the 20th Century.

00:01:57.683 --> 00:02:00.962
Today, with over $1.7 billion in annual sales,

00:02:01.044 --> 00:02:03.040
L.L. Bean remains one of the most

00:02:03.238 --> 00:02:05.770
successful family-run businesses in the United States.

00:02:07.538 --> 00:02:10.518
By following what excited him and by taking action

00:02:11.118 --> 00:02:13.778
LL Bean was able to transform himself from a man

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.391
who couldn’t hold down a steady job

00:02:15.572 --> 00:02:18.862
into one of the Top Ten Entrepreneurs of the 20th Century.

00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:20.967
To help you transform your business

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:24.339
here are 3 Action Items that you can learn from LL Bean.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.066
Action Item #1: Care for Your Customers

00:02:29.839 --> 00:02:31.874
If you want people to keep buying from you

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.634
and tell their friends to buy as well

00:02:33.857 --> 00:02:35.823
you need to care about their well-being

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:38.554
and provide as good an experience as possible for them.

00:02:38.781 --> 00:02:40.899
This is especially true in industries where there

00:02:41.107 --> 00:02:43.595
isn't really that much that's different between what you're offering

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:45.529
and what your competitor is selling.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.601
The differentiating factor that will make customers

00:02:48.016 --> 00:02:50.329
want to buy from you is the customer service

00:02:50.341 --> 00:02:52.301
and the experience that you give them.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.762
Bean's name became synonymous with outstanding

00:02:54.768 --> 00:02:55.736
customer service.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.703
One of his policies

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.496
was the 100% money back guarantee

00:02:59.661 --> 00:03:01.352
with no expiration date.

00:03:02.169 --> 00:03:04.072
No matter how long ago you bought his products

00:03:04.477 --> 00:03:06.197
Bean would refund you all of your money

00:03:06.458 --> 00:03:08.055
if you weren't completely satisfied.

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:09.896
He'd even pay for the postage

00:03:09.948 --> 00:03:10.945
for you to mail it back to him.

00:03:12.232 --> 00:03:13.461
Knowing that his customers were hunters

00:03:13.636 --> 00:03:14.494
and fishermen

00:03:14.636 --> 00:03:15.649
who often needed equipment

00:03:15.649 --> 00:03:16.717
in the middle of the night

00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:18.668
Bean also threw away the keys to his store

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.114
in Freeport and kept it open 24 hours a day

00:03:21.663 --> 00:03:24.943
365 days a year to give them a better experience.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:28.227
It's only been closed twice in its history.

00:03:29.114 --> 00:03:29.949
According to Bean

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.711
“No sale is really complete

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:33.457
until the product is worn out

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.166
and the customer is satisfied.

00:03:35.925 --> 00:03:39.042
A customer is the most important person ever in this office

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:40.705
in person or by mail.

00:03:41.739 --> 00:03:45.019
Above all, we wish to avoid having a dissatisfied customer.

00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:48.344
We consider our customers a part of our organization,

00:03:48.604 --> 00:03:51.425
and we want them to feel free to make any criticism

00:03:51.653 --> 00:03:54.426
they see fit in regard to our merchandise or service."

00:03:56.222 --> 00:03:57.576
Action Item #2:

00:03:58.107 --> 00:03:59.304
Be Your Target Market

00:03:59.659 --> 00:04:01.595
One of the best ways to do market research

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.744
and really know if you're on to something or not

00:04:04.054 --> 00:04:05.246
is to be your own customer.

00:04:06.038 --> 00:04:08.603
Does your product or service work as you would like it to?

00:04:09.324 --> 00:04:11.089
Would you be willing to pay money for it?

00:04:11.721 --> 00:04:13.047
Does it solve a real problem?

00:04:14.085 --> 00:04:15.598
The more you're a part of your target market

00:04:15.976 --> 00:04:17.903
the better chance you’ll have to create a product

00:04:18.134 --> 00:04:19.555
or service that will really sell.

00:04:20.146 --> 00:04:23.120
You'll know because it helps make what you're currently doing better

00:04:23.146 --> 00:04:23.565
faster

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.893
or somehow more effective.

00:04:26.123 --> 00:04:27.483
Bean's passion was hunting and fishing.

00:04:28.339 --> 00:04:30.371
It's what led him to create the Maine Hunting Shoe

00:04:30.871 --> 00:04:32.924
and kept him inspired to continue growing his business.

00:04:33.652 --> 00:04:36.445
Whether his executives wanted to launch a new fishing rod

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:37.172
shirt

00:04:37.411 --> 00:04:37.910
or tent

00:04:38.431 --> 00:04:41.322
Bean insisted on personally testing all of his products

00:04:41.691 --> 00:04:43.179
because it had his name on it

00:04:43.374 --> 00:04:45.276
and it needed his personal seal of approval.

00:04:46.164 --> 00:04:48.686
After the failure of his very first Maine Hunting Shoe

00:04:48.945 --> 00:04:51.577
he always took his products out into the real world

00:04:51.848 --> 00:04:54.271
to make sure they worked before they were sold

00:04:54.577 --> 00:04:56.334
even when his team around him advised

00:04:56.632 --> 00:04:58.452
that there were better uses of his time

00:04:58.792 --> 00:05:00.134
and someone else could do it.

00:05:01.238 --> 00:05:02.031
If it worked for him

00:05:02.064 --> 00:05:02.770
he knew his customers

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.602
would like it because he was one of them.

00:05:05.431 --> 00:05:06.558
Bean once wrote in his catalogue

00:05:06.937 --> 00:05:09.783
“It is no longer necessary for you to experiment

00:05:09.783 --> 00:05:12.900
with hundreds of flies to determine the few that will catch fish.

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.128
We’ve done that experimenting for you.”

00:05:15.628 --> 00:05:18.159
Bean continued being a part of his target market

00:05:18.415 --> 00:05:19.716
for as long as he could hold a fishing rod

00:05:19.873 --> 00:05:20.731
and lace up his boots.

00:05:23.251 --> 00:05:24.169
Action Item #3:

00:05:24.959 --> 00:05:25.519
Network

00:05:26.353 --> 00:05:27.841
Entrepreneurs often aren't great

00:05:28.081 --> 00:05:29.472
at promoting themselves and networking.

00:05:30.086 --> 00:05:32.543
Many of us are happiest when we're working on a new product

00:05:32.543 --> 00:05:34.401
or providing a service

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.289
instead of actually getting out there and selling.

00:05:37.064 --> 00:05:38.083
But getting your product or service

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.582
into the hands of the right people

00:05:39.795 --> 00:05:41.655
can often make or break your company

00:05:41.685 --> 00:05:43.283
and you need to be an effective networker

00:05:43.463 --> 00:05:44.882
to make sure that they know what you've got!

00:05:46.532 --> 00:05:48.165
Bean was always an outdoorsman at heart

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.748
but he knew how to network and promote his business.

00:05:51.616 --> 00:05:53.747
After the avid hunters started buying his products

00:05:54.477 --> 00:05:56.643
Bean made a point of connecting with high profile people

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.535
to introduce them to his company.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.517
Everyone from Franklin Roosevelt to Babe Ruth

00:06:01.855 --> 00:06:05.068
to John Wayne found out about his products and began using them.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.090
Bean also sponsored high profile athletes

00:06:08.754 --> 00:06:11.576
like the 1932 Macmillan Arctic Expedition team

00:06:12.005 --> 00:06:13.804
who wore his boots on their expedition.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.176
But you didn't have to be famous for Bean

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:17.610
to let you know what he did.

00:06:18.527 --> 00:06:20.519
As one local writer from Maine wrote of Bean

00:06:21.053 --> 00:06:22.847
“If you drop in to shake his hand

00:06:23.423 --> 00:06:25.942
you get home to find his catalogue in your mailbox.”

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:28.715
So remember;

00:06:29.052 --> 00:06:30.074
care for your customers

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:33.193
be your target market, and network.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:35.050
To finish up this video

00:06:35.419 --> 00:06:37.341
I wanted to share one of my favorite true stories

00:06:37.517 --> 00:06:39.665
about LL Bean and some of his best quotes.

00:06:42.354 --> 00:06:44.402
When Bean first threw away the keys to his store

00:06:44.614 --> 00:06:46.962
and invited hunters and fishermen to come visit the store

00:06:47.276 --> 00:06:48.116
whenever they wanted

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:49.978
he installed a late night bell

00:06:50.168 --> 00:06:51.637
to allow people to ring for assistance.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.885
Customers who arrived late at night

00:06:54.026 --> 00:06:55.722
would see the bell and a sign that read:

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.802
“Push once a minute until clerk appears.”

00:06:58.915 --> 00:07:00.242
Pushing the bell would bring a watchman

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:03.451
and often even Bean himself to come help the customer

00:07:03.583 --> 00:07:04.777
no matter what time of day it was. 


00:07:46.909 --> 00:07:49.159
Thank you for joining me for another edition of

00:07:49.159 --> 00:07:50.048
Modeling the Masters.

